-msgid "On a display that takes no HDR, an HDR video is converted to ordinary SDR (Dolby Vision always; HDR10, HDR10+ and HLG with the tone mapping method \"Reference (BT.2390)\", the default), and this says what kind of display that SDR is made for. Reference (the default): a display that shows white at 203 cd/m² with gamma 2.4, as the standards define for SDR made from HDR. Bright room: a display set brighter, white at 300 cd/m² with gamma 2.2, as many TVs in a lit living room: choose it if the picture looks too bright or washed out with Reference. Projector: a dimmer display, white at 100 cd/m²: choose it if the picture looks too dark with Reference. Custom: the white and the gamma that you set below. Nothing is clipped in any of them: what is brighter than the display's white is compressed. Applies from the next video."
